  "hypothesis": {
    "id": "steer-path-fixed-overhead-ablation",
    "parent": "steer-term-zero-weight-shortcircuit",
    "kind": "ablate",
    "title": "Bisect the residual steer-path overhead with the active-term slice empty",
    "description": "With the landed empty-slice fast path in place, ablate the remaining steer plumbing one stage at a time and measure each in isolation: (a) skip materialising the candidate/ready-set that is built for the scorer in spur-core/src/simulator/core/scheduler.rs before the steer call; (b) skip all utilStats.steerAuthority accumulation in spur-core/src/simulator/util_stats.rs when active_terms == 0; (c) hoist the scorer call boundary itself (and any state/path snapshot it touches in core/state.rs and simulator/path.rs) out of the step loop when the slice is empty. Each ablation is a separate build behind the existing steer_terms block in scheduler_configs/loop/general_vr.json -- no new config key. Validation: 300 s single-arm runs, seed 1000, rayon 30, all weights 0, compared against arm-000 (389 runs/s) and the no-steer baseline median (575 runs/s); report runs/s per ablation so the 27-point residual is attributed to one or more stages. Accept the stage whose ablation recovers >= 15% on its own and re-check bit-identity at a nonzero arm (339,717 expressed / 119,762 honored).",
    "category": "performance",
    "buildsOn": [
      "steer_terms",
      "active-term slice",
      "campaign arm overlays"
    ],
    "expectedGain": 6,
    "expectedCost": 1.5,
    "rationale": "The predicate short-circuit proved only 5.7% of a 33% gap, so ~27 points are still unlocated and are paid by every steer campaign regardless of weights. Measuring per stage instead of guessing avoids a second 6-file change that buys 5%; whichever stage dominates is then a cheap targeted fix, and restoring the steer path to >= 0.8 of baseline is what makes the factorial affordable enough to beat its 3.5% counting noise.",
    "generalityArgument": "Pure measurement plus dead-work elimination in the scheduler's own bookkeeping. It names no handler, message, role or protocol, and every ablation is required to leave the schedule bit-identical at nonzero weights.",
    "status": "proposed",
    "branch": null,
    "prUrls": [],
    "createdAtIso": "2026-08-29T08:10:00Z",
    "firingCounter": null,
    "notes": "Arm 000 is not 'steering off' -- it is the full plumbing minus the inner loop. Keep a true no-steer-block build as the control in every comparison. [rejudged iteration 5316: Up-scored: the zero-weight shortcircuit closure localised ~27 of the 33 throughput points to fixed per-step steer plumbing the empty-slice path still pays, which is a named hotspot with a >=15-30% expected runs/s delta and no "
